WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.160
This film is the story of Loung Ung when she was a little girl.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.760
It's her experience during the war.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.440
And Loung is a dear friend of mine who I met over 15 years ago.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.780
Reading her book taught me a lot about this country

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.240
So in a way, I'm doing this for her, for her family, for Cambodia

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.900
And very much so, also for Maddox, so he learns about who he is and knows who his people are.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:37.180
This is the story of, not just my family, but it's the story of a nation.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.500
I wasn't going to trust it to anybody

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.420
Maddox has been working on this since the beginning — he's in the production...

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.880
He helped me with the script.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.660
And it isn't just because he's my son.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:10.740
It's because this film is through the eyes of a child and we've all had to open up a little bit more and be like children.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.340
I didn't want to see a child go through war.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.540
I wanted to know what a child felt and what they focused on, what they saw.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.900
If you know nothing about Cambodia, and you see this film

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.240
you won't just think, "These are people that suffered through a war."

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.380
You will think, "These are really interesting people."

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:06.160
Their roots and their personality, their humor, their love of music, their culture, It's all of that.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:11.560
It has to be, in the end, this love letter to Cambodian people.

